<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Cornus controversa)",
        "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Cornus controversa morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Cornus controversa specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Cornus controversa" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A fossil predecessor inside this 1/1 chronoseries",
        "does_not_claim: That pagoda tiers are chemical stripes",
        "does_not_claim: That the Variegata cream margin is a Turing pattern",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Early-time mode growth, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Slot-specific rates a=0.06, b=0.94 and the diffusivities that pin lambda_c = 1.939 mm",
        "reported_in_source: Public-domain Meise Botanic Garden photograph of C. controversa 'Variegata'",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and the diffusion-driven instability conditions",
        "reported_in_source: Xiang et al. 2006 place Cornus controversa in extant Cornus; this chronoseries is the Holocene tip only",
        "transfer_boundary: Crown pixels are used for orientation and occupancy, not for a millimetre reading",
        "transfer_boundary: The 1.939 mm length is the Delphi detail-scale assignment, not a published Cornus measurement" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Cornus controversa; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and the diffusion-driven instability conditions | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Xiang et al. 2006 place Cornus controversa in extant Cornus; this chronoseries is the Holocene tip only | Public-domain Meise Botanic Garden photograph of C. controversa 'Variegata'; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-specific rates a=0.06, b=0.94 and the diffusivities that pin lambda_c = 1.939 mm | Early-time mode growth, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation; transfer_boundary: The 1.939 mm length is the Delphi detail-scale assignment, not a published Cornus measurement | Crown pixels are used for orientation and occupancy, not for a millimetre reading; does_not_claim: That the Variegata cream margin is a Turing pattern | That pagoda tiers are chemical stripes | A fossil predecessor inside this 1/1 chronoseries]; phenomenon_size: 2.0 cm (0.01995 m, log10=-1.7 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 2.0 cm to 2.0 cm): 2.0 cm:dichotomous-tree-branching" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lfs.2005.05.094>,
