<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "jacobian, solve_diffusivities, growth_rate, integrate, and ablation_control are named for equations (1)–(6). The Lean module uses the same scaled integers (trace -120 per thousand, wavelength product 1939*3240, equal-diffusion contrast). The proofs are kernel `decide` witnesses on those integers, not a formal PDE." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Equations (1)–(6) in the module docstring are the Schnakenberg PDE, the steady state, the Jacobian, and Turing's k_c. solve_diffusivities returns lambda = 1.939000 mm and a self-test checks trace < 0, det > 0, Dv > Du, and a closed band when Du = Dv. Modes whose eigenvalues are a complex pair are excluded, because |u-hat| is then not a pure exponential; the eleven real modes that remain track sigma(k). Deduction: a and b were chosen for this slot so the wavelength would land on 1.939 mm. They are not parameters reported for Cornus." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Linear probe: Pearson r = 0.9999998 (n = 11 real modes), RMSE = 2.13e-4 per time unit, against reference bar 0.98. KS statistic of the residuals versus Normal(0, s) is 0.514 (p = 0.003): the residuals are structured truncation error, not a normal sample, and that failure is reported rather than dropped. Nonlinear dominant wavelength on the 8-lambda box is 2.216 mm versus 1.939 mm (ratio 1.14), i.e. Fourier bin 7 instead of bin 8. Ablation std ratio 0.018 with sigma_max -0.0615. Specimen foreground 0.866 versus null 0.50, foliage fraction 0.212 versus null 0.25, horizontal-edge fraction 0.433 versus the field's 0.421. The crown frame is 960x1280 and has no scale bar, so none of those photo numbers is a millimetre. The resolution block is not written on this pass." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ablation-equal-diffusion-std-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-pearson-r-pde-vs-analytic-sigma>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-nonlinear-dominant-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-foliage-bright-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-horizontal-edge-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 82.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg kinetics with a=0.06, b=0.94 (trace -0.120, det 1) and diffusivities solved so the continuum critical wavelength is 1.939 mm (0.001939 m, log10 -2.712). Eleven real-eigenvalue Fourier modes give Pearson r = 0.9999998 and RMSE = 2.13e-4 against analytic sigma(k). The equal-diffusion control has sigma_max = -0.0615 and std ratio 0.018. A Dv sweep from 0.65 to 2.4 times nominal moves lambda monotonically from 1.998 mm to 1.881 mm. The saturated 8-wavelength patch peaks at 2.216 mm, the neighboring Fourier bin. The crown photograph has no scale bar. PASS2_REMEDIATION is False, so the 16-wavelength remeasure, the horizontal bias, and the resolution block are not in this run. Weighted score 82.7/100. Overall 82.7/100 (faithfulness 81.3, reproducibility 86.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 336856 B, 1260×840 px, artifact_sha256 18349142d83a189347f1985eaa85597ad380c86887a617c474e816d962a6cd9a (sha256 18349142d83a189347f1985eaa85597ad380c86887a617c474e816d962a6cd9a), spec_fingerprint 889436d47b7f6a20b524144198f645dcccbc348d99fd9ce666f715dfafc2a48a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 889436d47b7f6a20b524144198f645dcccbc348d99fd9ce666f715dfafc2a48a; artifact_sha256: 18349142d83a189347f1985eaa85597ad380c86887a617c474e816d962a6cd9a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0/cornus_controversa_specimen.jpg=be3da2bb8b817bec..., datasets/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0/cornus_controversa_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=61581ec4249a6ec3...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and the diffusion-driven instability conditions | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Xiang et al. 2006 place Cornus controversa in extant Cornus; this chronoseries is the Holocene tip only | Public-domain Meise Botanic Garden photograph of C. controversa 'Variegata'; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-specific rates a=0.06, b=0.94 and the diffusivities that pin lambda_c = 1.939 mm | Early-time mode growth, Dv sweep, and equal-diffusion ablation; transfer_boundary: The 1.939 mm length is the Delphi detail-scale assignment, not a published Cornus measurement | Crown pixels are used for orientation and occupancy, not for a millimetre reading; does_not_claim: That the Variegata cream margin is a Turing pattern | That pagoda tiers are chemical stripes | A fossil predecessor inside this 1/1 chronoseries." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Nonlinear peak is 2.216 mm on the 8-wavelength box (Fourier bin 7). Re-measure on a 16-wavelength patch before treating 1.939 mm as the saturated wavelength.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Horizontal midrib bias is implemented but PASS2_REMEDIATION is False, so orientation is not exercised as a parameter.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'resolution_limit is null. Record that the crown photograph has no scale bar and that 1.939 mm is not read off those pixels.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': \"No second assessor. This score is the builder's own.\"}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml. Do not invent a signature.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.27e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "lambda_of_dv moves monotonically as Dv/Dv* runs through 0.65, 0.80, 1.00, 1.35, 1.80, 2.40: wavelengths 1.998, 1.966, 1.939, 1.913, 1.894, 1.881 mm. The nominal factor returns the assignment. The equal-diffusion ablation is a separate switch, not a point on that curve. The horizontal bias exists in integrate() but PASS2_REMEDIATION is False, so this pass does not exercise it." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0.py L82–L83: Pass 1 executed with the remediation flag off, so the midrib template was not applied <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc/models/2026-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L82-L83>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cornus-controversa-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cornus controversa Turing wavenumber at 1.939 mm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Reproducibility package: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "--self-test checks the hash, the band, the monotonic sweep, Pearson r > 0.98, RMSE < 0.05, and the decaying ablation. Seed is 3155. Full run writes the PNG, the 12-frame GIF, and the metrics JSON. Deduction: dependency versions are the environment's scientific stack, not a per-script lockfile, and the checkpoint commit does not yet contain these new paths." ;
